   "id": "shabbat.54b.10",
   "daf": "54b",
   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "וְלֹא בִּרְצוּעָה: דְּעָבְדִי לְהוּ כִּי הֵיכִי דְּלָא לִיתְבְּרוּ מָאנֵי. וְאֵין הַזְּכָרִים יוֹצְאִין בָּעֲגָלָה: כִּי הֵיכִי דְּלָא לִחְמְטָן אַלְיָיתַיְהוּ.",
   "en": "The mishna continues: «Nor with a strap» on their feet. The Gemara explains that the owner «does» so «to» the roosters «so that they will not break vessels.» When their legs are tied, they jump around less and cause less damage. The mishna teaches: «Rams may not go out with a» small «wagon» under their tails. The Gemara explains that these wagons were placed there «in order that their tails will not be injured.»"
  }
 ],
